      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-286202",
      ":question/problem": "A diver jumps from a platform into a pool. Her height, in meters above the water, is modeled by a quadratic function of the time, in seconds, since she left the platform. According to the model, she jumped from a height of $10$ meters above the water and reached her highest point of $11.5$ meters after $0.5$ seconds. After how many seconds does the model predict she will hit the water? (Round to the nearest whole number)"
