      ":question/problem": "A skier launches off a ramp into the air. Her height, in meters above the ground, is modeled by a quadratic function of the time, in seconds, since she left the ramp. According to the model, she launched from a height of $8$ meters above the ground and reached her highest point of $17$ meters after $3$ seconds. After how many seconds does the model predict she will land? (Round to the nearest whole number)"
